WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:17.805
practiced with Dirk in her driveway until dark.

2
00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:23.948
Then someone on a bike rode past.

3
00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:29.191
"Hey, Brooklyn, want to ride to the Ice Cream Hut?"

4
00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:30.392
Jacey asked.

5
00:00:31.256 --> 00:00:33.917
Suddenly she noticed Dirk under the basketball hoop.

6
00:00:33.937 --> 00:00:36.398
"Dirk! Why are you here?"

7
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:38.119
"I can't right now.

8
00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:41.300
We're practicing for tomorrow's game," Brooklyn answered.

9
00:00:42.581 --> 00:00:45.522
Dirk wiped sweat from his forehead without looking at Jacey.

10
00:00:47.023 --> 00:00:51.064
He spun around under the net and jumped up, nailing a slam dunk.

11
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:55.546
"I can't go either," Dirk said.

12
00:00:55.566 --> 00:00:57.647
"I'm going to talk to Marv soon."

13
00:00:58.507 --> 00:01:00.028
Brooklyn ran to grab the ball.

14
00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.669
"Jacey, watch this cool move."

15
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.832
Jacey watched Dirk for only a few seconds.

16
00:01:08.572 --> 00:01:11.214
Then she rode off on her bike without looking back.

17
00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.175
"See you guys tomorrow."

18
00:01:15.917 --> 00:01:19.059
Brooklyn arrived at the gym extra early on Saturday morning.

19
00:01:21.641 --> 00:01:24.863
But someone else had obviously arrived even earlier.

20
00:01:25.964 --> 00:01:30.968
A large sign hung above the spectators' section: Sit here, Brooklyn.

21
00:01:31.464 --> 00:01:32.665
You're no coach!

22
00:01:33.566 --> 00:01:35.267
Brooklyn gasped in surprise.

23
00:01:37.048 --> 00:01:40.030
Someone had gone to a lot of trouble to intimidate her.

24
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:44.593
"That stupid sign doesn't bother me at all," she said out loud.

25
00:01:44.613 --> 00:01:47.675
"It just makes me more determined to win!"

26
00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:52.258
that, Brooklyn?"

27
00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.600
She was ripping down the sign when Marv entered the gym.

28
00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.003
"Nothing." Brooklyn crumpled up the paper.

29
00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:02.889
"It's something."

30
00:02:03.749 --> 00:02:04.850
Marv walked closer.

31
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:09.213
"Or you wouldn't be hiding it from me.

32
00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:10.754
Show it to me, please."

33
00:02:11.755 --> 00:02:16.238
She stepped off the bleachers and reluctantly spread the crumpled sign on the gym floor.

34
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.041
Marv read the words and began pacing.

35
00:02:24.884 --> 00:02:26.765
someone on the team bullying you?"

36
00:02:26.785 --> 00:02:30.888
"I've gotten a few messages," Brooklyn said softly.

37
00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:32.713
"I can handle it, Marv."

38
00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:35.054
Marv stopped pacing.

39
00:02:35.074 --> 00:02:41.016
"I believe you can handle it, Brooklyn, but that doesn't make it okay.

40
00:02:41.756 --> 00:02:44.377
Bullying violates our team and school rules."

41
00:02:45.638 --> 00:02:49.079
"I thought I knew who was sending me the notes, but I was wrong."

42
00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.300
Marv picked up the sign.

43
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.882
"Always let people know if you're being bullied.

44
00:02:55.462 --> 00:02:57.623
I'll show this to the principal when she arrives.

45
00:02:58.523 --> 00:03:00.384
Right now let's prepare for the game."

46
00:03:01.024 --> 00:03:03.186
He started toward the gym office with the sign.

47
00:03:03.206 --> 00:03:09.490
"Please don't say anything to the players yet," Brooklyn said.

48
00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.971
"The team has to focus on the game."

49
00:03:13.773 --> 00:03:14.573
Marv smiled.

50
00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:17.075
"You really are a good coach, Brooklyn.

51
00:03:17.555 --> 00:03:19.837
You're always thinking about what's best for the team."

52
00:03:21.158 --> 00:03:22.999
Dirk was the first player to arrive.

53
00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.162
When Marv came out of the office, Dirk pumped a fist in the air.

54
00:03:27.182 --> 00:03:30.344
"Whales Whoosh!"

55
00:03:31.388 --> 00:03:32.289
"Whales Whoosh!"

56
00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:34.830
Marv said, and Brooklyn joined in.

57
00:03:38.371 --> 00:03:42.333
Noise quickly filled the gym as more players and spectators arrived.

58
00:03:42.773 --> 00:03:45.475
Brooklyn felt butterflies fluttering in her stomach.

59
00:03:46.135 --> 00:03:48.076
The Whales had to win today!

60
00:03:51.177 --> 00:03:56.179
In the first minute of the game, the Terriers' giant guard raced down the court and stole the

61
00:03:56.199 --> 00:04:04.080
ball from Jacey.

62
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.221
He immediately scored.

63
00:04:06.322 --> 00:04:08.363
Jacey looked as if she might cry.

64
00:04:08.383 --> 00:04:12.446
"Shake it off, Jacey," Brooklyn called.

65
00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.568
Jacey glanced at Dirk, who was sitting on the bench.

66
00:04:16.649 --> 00:04:17.670
"Listen to Brooklyn!"

67
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:18.650
he shouted.

68
00:04:19.331 --> 00:04:20.532
Stuart had the ball now.

69
00:04:22.693 --> 00:04:24.154
The referee blew his whistle.

70
00:04:24.174 --> 00:04:28.177
"Foul! Traveling!"

71
00:04:29.177 --> 00:04:30.578
Marv nodded at Brooklyn.

72
00:04:31.359 --> 00:04:35.065
Stuart was traveling, just as she had pointed out in practice.

73
00:04:35.826 --> 00:04:37.887
Seconds later Stuart had the ball again.

74
00:04:37.907 --> 00:04:41.168
"Dribble!" Brooklyn shouted.

75
00:04:41.649 --> 00:04:44.590
This time Stuart kept dribbling as he ran toward the net.

76
00:04:48.432 --> 00:04:52.214
He missed the shot, but Jacey grabbed the ball and sunk a basket.

77
00:04:58.418 --> 00:04:59.658
Brooklyn pumped her fist.

78
00:05:00.639 --> 00:05:04.576
Both teams raced up and down the court, scoring point after point.

79
00:05:12.038 --> 00:05:15.039
Brooklyn paced the sideline with Marv, calling to players.

80
00:05:15.059 --> 00:05:18.880
"Aaron, try a low pass!"

81
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.341
"Loop it, Jacey!"

82
00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:22.361
"Way to steal, Stuart!"

83
00:05:23.361 --> 00:05:25.902
Brooklyn was pleased to see the players listening to her.

84
00:05:27.002 --> 00:05:32.184
But when she offered Jacey a cold water bottle, her friend wouldn't take it, or even look at

85
00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:35.898
her. "Great fake before that three-pointer, Jacey."

86
00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:38.881
"You're not our coach," Jacey muttered.

87
00:05:39.702 --> 00:05:40.783
The comment stung.

88
00:05:42.224 --> 00:05:46.428
Brooklyn swallowed, trying to keep her mind on the game instead of Jacey.

89
00:05:49.771 --> 00:05:53.995
At halftime the score was tied: 24-24.

90
00:05:54.936 --> 00:05:58.600
Marv and Brooklyn were planning plays when the Terriers coach approached.

91
00:06:01.244 --> 00:06:03.706
"I found this envelope by the Whales' cooler.

92
00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:05.808
Belong to anybody on the team?"

93
00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:09.891
Brooklyn's name was on the front of the envelope.

94
00:06:10.892 --> 00:06:18.338
She opened it, her hands shaking, and read the note inside: You'll always be a clumsy loser.

95
00:06:19.339 --> 00:06:22.321
So far Brooklyn hadn't let the notes bother her.

96
00:06:22.922 --> 00:06:25.524
But this one made tears spring to her eyes.

97
00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:27.846
Marv gave her his handkerchief.

98
00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:29.647
"Don't worry.

99
00:06:29.807 --> 00:06:31.989
It's clean," he joked softly.

100
00:06:32.829 --> 00:06:34.350
He led her to the team bench.

101
00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.111
"Take slow, deep breaths.

102
00:06:37.831 --> 00:06:40.732
After the game I'm showing this note to the principal too.

103
00:06:41.653 --> 00:06:43.053
The bully will be punished.

104
00:06:43.574 --> 00:06:46.355
But right now, kid, I need your coaching help."

105
00:06:47.335 --> 00:06:49.016
Brooklyn sniffled and nodded.

106
00:06:50.177 --> 00:06:51.597
Marv waved over the players.

107
00:06:51.617 --> 00:06:53.438
"Gather round, Whales."

108
00:06:54.559 --> 00:06:56.319
Aaron saw Brooklyn wiping her eyes.

109
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.640
"What's wrong?"

110
00:06:59.124 --> 00:07:03.126
"It looks like someone on our team is bullying Brooklyn," Marv said.

111
00:07:03.146 --> 00:07:05.948
"Huh?" a few players said.

112
00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:08.589
"Is this about those messages?"

113
00:07:09.049 --> 00:07:09.790
Jacey asked.

114
00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:14.192
"Brooklyn, maybe you shouldn't coach us today if you're really upset."

115
00:07:15.213 --> 00:07:16.594
Dirk gave Jacey a look.

116
00:07:16.614 --> 00:07:18.795
"Brooklyn is helping our team."

117
00:07:18.815 --> 00:07:21.136
"Yeah," said Stuart.

118
00:07:21.656 --> 00:07:24.498
"She knew when I had an opening to steal in the second quarter."

119
00:07:24.518 --> 00:07:28.200
"Her tips totally helped my dribbling," said Aaron.

120
00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:33.042
"Marv has a lot more experience," Jacey said sharply.

121
00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:35.444
Brooklyn's tears had dried.

122
00:07:36.384 --> 00:07:42.848
She suddenly pictured Jacey on her bike yesterday Jacey's frown when Brooklyn and Dirk didn't stop practicing to

123
00:07:42.888 --> 00:07:44.109
go to the Ice Cream Hut.

124
00:07:44.689 --> 00:07:45.910
Was Jacey jealous?

125
00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:50.773
"Brooklyn will stay and help me," Marv said sternly.

126
00:07:50.793 --> 00:07:54.075
"But Jacey, you can leave right now.

127
00:07:55.296 --> 00:07:59.970
In fact, maybe you'd like to go talk to the principal about that sign you made."

128
00:08:00.991 --> 00:08:06.314
Jacey's mouth opened and shut, like a goldfish out of its bowl gasping in the air.

129
00:08:07.494 --> 00:08:10.236
Brooklyn had guessed at the same time as Marv.

130
00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:12.737
"Did you write those notes to me?"

131
00:08:13.197 --> 00:08:14.078
she blurted out.

132
00:08:15.318 --> 00:08:16.559
Jacey didn't answer.

133
00:08:17.219 --> 00:08:18.940
She just ran out of the gym.

134
00:08:23.303 --> 00:08:25.584
The buzzer sounded to start the second half.

135
00:08:26.476 --> 00:08:27.597
"Play smart, Whales!"

136
00:08:28.077 --> 00:08:28.737
Marv said.

137
00:08:29.377 --> 00:08:31.578
Brooklyn stood, her legs wobbling.

138
00:08:32.299 --> 00:08:33.599
Jacey was her friend.

139
00:08:34.399 --> 00:08:37.021
How could she "Focus!"

140
00:08:37.521 --> 00:08:39.242
Brooklyn told herself fiercely.

141
00:08:39.262 --> 00:08:41.583
"That's what coaches do!"

142
00:08:43.123 --> 00:08:46.225
The Whales and Terriers continued battling for points.

143
00:08:47.205 --> 00:08:52.987
With forty seconds left on the clock, Dirk whipped around under the net to slam-dunk a shot and

144
00:08:53.067 --> 00:08:54.028
tie up the game.

145
00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:04.326
The next time Aaron had the ball, the frustrated Terriers' giant fouled, bumping hard into Aaron.

146
00:09:08.407 --> 00:09:11.908
Now the Whales had a free throw they could take the lead!

147
00:09:13.088 --> 00:09:15.869
Aaron stepped up for the shot—and missed.

148
00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.330
Brooklyn groaned.

149
00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.592
The clock ticked down to twenty seconds as a Terrier raced downcourt with the ball.

150
00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.741
Dirk signaled Stuart.

151
00:09:30.761 --> 00:09:33.223
"Yes!" Brooklyn whispered.

152
00:09:33.243 --> 00:09:34.964
"It's time to try it!"

153
00:09:35.985 --> 00:09:40.988
She hoped her practice with Dirk the Jedi would pay off before the final buzzer.
